{"text": "Wrong Number.\n\nOn Saturday morning, there was still no photo.\n\nMateo went slowly to the kitchen. \"Mum, the photos stopped,\" he said.\n\n\"You miss them,\" said Mum with a small smile.\n\n\"Maybe,\" said Mateo. \"Can I write to the number now? Just one message?\"\n\n\"OK. But we write it together. And no names.\"\n\nMateo quickly typed, \"wrong nr pls dont stop.\"\n\nMum shook her head. \"This is a stranger, not Rui. Write real sentences, please.\"\n\nSo Mateo wrote it again, slowly and carefully.\n\n\"Hello. I'm sorry, but this is the wrong number. Please don't stop, because I love your photos.\"\n\nHe sent it. Then he waited.\n\nAn hour later, the phone made a sound.\n\n\"Oh no! I'm so sorry!\" the message said. \"My sister moved to another country in May. She got a new number. So I sent my photos to you!\"\n\nThen another message came. \"Do you like the sea?\"\n\nMateo looked at Mum. \"I love it,\" he wrote. \"But I broke my leg. I can't go out this summer.\"\n\n\"Poor you!\" came the answer. \"Then I'm going to send you the sea every morning. Is that OK?\"\n\nMateo smiled for the first time in a week. \"Yes, please,\" he wrote.\n\nSo the photos started again. Now there were words with them, too.\n\n\"Look, dolphins! Three of them came very close today.\"\n\n\"This red boat goes out at six. The old fisherman always waves.\"\n\n\"The water is colder today, so only two people swam.\"\n\nMateo read every message to Mum at breakfast.\n\n\"How does this person know about the swimmers?\" asked Mum.\n\n\"Maybe they live near the beach,\" said Mateo.\n\nThe stranger never asked for Mateo's name or address. Mum liked that.\n\nMateo asked questions, too. \"Why do you get up so early?\"\n\n\"Because I work at the beach,\" came the answer. \"My job is to watch the sea.\"\n\nOne morning, the photo was different. On the left, there were houses on the hill.\n\n\"Good morning!\" said the message. \"Today I can see a yellow house with a blue balcony. It's the brightest house on the hill.\"\n\nMateo looked at the photo. Then he looked out of his window.\n\nThe yellow house was his house. The blue balcony was his balcony.\n\nHe went to the kitchen as quickly as he could.\n\n\"Mum! The stranger can see our house!\"", "textSha256": "3824c5eb8d73d925f92a1d293072e4c914116300f01bfcf209f34246bc5380e6", "voice_id": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "speed": 0.95, "lang": "en", "parts": 1, "alignment": {"characters": ["W", "r", "o", "n", "g", " ", "N", "u", "m", "b", "e", "r", ".", "\n", "\n", "O", "n", " ", "S", "a", "t", "u", "r", "d", "a", "y", " ", "m", "o", "r", "n", "i", "n", "g", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", "r", "e", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "s", "t", "i", "l", "l", " ", "n", "o", " ", "p", "h", "o", "t", "o", ".", "\n", "\n", "M", "a", "t", "e", "o", " ", "w", "e", "n", "t", " ", "s", "l", "o", "w", "l", "y", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "k", "i", "t", "c", "h", "e", "n", ".", " ", "\"", "M", "u", "m", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "p", "h", "o", "t", "o", "s", " ", "s", "t", "o", "p", "p", "e", "d", ",", "\"", " ", "h", "e", " ", "s", "a", "i", "d", ".", "\n", "\n", "\"", "Y", "o", "u", " ", "m", "i", "s", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", "m", ",", "\"", " ", "s", "a", "i", "d", " ", "M", "u", "m", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", " ", "a", " ", "s", "m", "a", "l", "l", " ", "s", "m", "i", "l", "e", ".", "\n", "\n", "\"", "M", "a", "y", "b", "e", ",", "\"", " ", "s", "a", "i", "d", " ", "M", "a", "t", "e", "o", ".", " ", "\"", "C", "a", "n", " ", "I", " ", "w", "r", "i", "t", "e", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "n", "u", "m", "b", "e", "r", " ", "n", "o", "w", "?", " ", "J", "u", "s", "t", " ", "o", "n", "e", " ", "m", "e", "s", "s", "a", "g", "e", "?", "\"", "\n", "\n", "\"", "O", "K", ".", " ", "B", "u", "t", " ", "w", "e", " ", "w", "r", "i", "t", "e", " ", "i", "t", " ", "t", "o", "g", "e", "t", "h", "e", "r", ".", " ", "A", "n", "d", " ", "n", "o", " ", "n", "a", "m", "e", "s", ".", "\"", "\n", "\n", "M", 